{
    "map": {
        "alignment_feature.descr": "The line feature that will be used to align the orientation of the regularized polygons. Each polygon will only be aligned to one line feature.",
        "alignment_feature.title": "Alignment Feature",
        "alignment_tolerance.descr": "The maximum distance threshold that will be used for finding the nearest alignment feature. For example, a value of 20 meters means the nearest line that is within 20 meters will be used to align the regularized polygon.",
        "alignment_tolerance.title": "Alignment Tolerance",
        "densification.descr": "<xdoc><p>The sampling interval that will be used to evaluate whether the regularized feature will be straight or bent. The densification must be equal to or less than the tolerance value.</p><p>This parameter is only used with methods that support right angle identification.</p></xdoc>",
        "densification.title": "Densification",
        "description": "Normalizes the footprint of building polygons by eliminating undesirable artifacts in their geometry.",
        "diagonal_penalty.descr": "<xdoc><p>When the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Right Angles and Diagonals</span> method is used, this value identifies the likelihood of constructing right angles or diagonal edges between two adjoining segments. When the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Any Angles</span> method is used, this value identifies the likelihood of constructing diagonal edges that do not conform to the preferred edges determined by the tool&apos;s algorithm. If the penalty value is set to 0, the preferred edges will not be used, resulting in the production of a simplified irregular polygon. Generally, the higher the value, the less likely a diagonal edge will be constructed.</p></xdoc>",
        "diagonal_penalty.title": "Diagonal Penalty",
        "in_features.descr": "The polygons that represent the building footprints to be regularized.",
        "in_features.title": "Input Features",
        "max_radius.descr": "<xdoc><p>The largest radius allowed for a regularized circle. This option is only available with the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Circle</span> method.</p></xdoc>",
        "max_radius.title": "Maximum Radius",
        "method.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the regularization method that will be used in processing the input features.</p><ul><li><span title=\"RIGHT_ANGLES\">Right Angles</span>—Shapes composed of 90° angles between adjoining edges will be constructed.</li><li><span title=\"RIGHT_ANGLES_AND_DIAGONALS\">Right Angles and Diagonals</span>—Shapes composed of 45° and 90° angles between adjoining edges will be constructed.</li><li><span title=\"ANY_ANGLE\">Any Angles</span>—Shapes that form any angles between adjoining edges will be constructed.</li><li><span title=\"CIRCLE\">Circle</span>—The best fitting circle around the input features will be constructed.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "method.domain.ANY_ANGLE": "Any Angles",
        "method.domain.CIRCLE": "Circle",
        "method.domain.RIGHT_ANGLES": "Right Angles",
        "method.domain.RIGHT_ANGLES_AND_DIAGONALS": "Right Angles and Diagonals",
        "method.title": "Method",
        "min_radius.descr": "<xdoc><p>The smallest radius allowed for a regularized circle. A value of 0 implies that there is no minimum size limit. This option is only available with the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Circle</span> method.</p></xdoc>",
        "min_radius.title": "Minimum Radius",
        "out_feature_class.descr": "The feature class that will be produced.",
        "out_feature_class.title": "Output Feature Class",
        "precision.descr": "The precision of the spatial grid that will be used in the regularization process. Valid values range from 0.05 to 0.25.",
        "precision.title": "Precision",
        "title": "Regularize Building Footprint",
        "tolerance.descr": "<xdoc><p>For most methods, this value represents the maximum distance that the regularized footprint can deviate from the boundary of its originating feature. The specified value will be based on the linear units of the input feature&apos;s coordinate system. When using the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Circle</span> method, this option can also be interpreted as a ratio of the difference between the original feature and its regularized result against the area of the regularized result based on the selection that is made in the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Tolerance Type</span> parameter.</p></xdoc>",
        "tolerance.title": "Tolerance",
        "tolerance_type.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies how tolerance will be applied when the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Method</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Circle</span>.</p><ul><li><span title=\"DISTANCE\">Distance</span>—The tolerance will represent the maximum distance from the boundary of the feature being processed. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"AREA_RATIO\">Area Ratio</span>—The tolerance will represent the maximum limit for the ratio between the area of the original feature that differs from the regularized circle and the area of the regularized circle.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "tolerance_type.domain.AREA_RATIO": "Area Ratio",
        "tolerance_type.domain.DISTANCE": "Distance",
        "tolerance_type.title": "Tolerance Type"
    }
}
